// Puzzle data for Outwit, the daily crowd game. SERVER-ONLY: imported by
// app/outwit/page.js (which strips answers/house before the client sees it)
// and by app/api/outwit/route.js (which scores against house + real picks).
// The `house` arrays are the pre-written "house crowd" (~48 answers per
// prompt) that seeds each day's pool so the first player at 12:01am faces a
// realistic field. For choice AND unique prompts, house entries are OPTION INDICES.
// Generated by a seeded script (deterministic); hand-shaped distributions.
// When banking more days: keep prompt types + order (least, herd, match,
// unique, twothirds — unique is a themed 8-option rarest-pick prompt, and the
// twothirds "Undercut" prompt runs LAST), write fresh flavor, and re-shape house
// arrays to plausible crowd behavior for the new questions. Truth/truthNote
// power the herd reveal.
//
// UNDERCUT FRACTION MOVES DAILY (owner rule, 2026-07-20): the Undercut prompt is
// no longer always two-thirds of the average. Each day carries an explicit
// `frac` (and matching `fracLabel` / question copy) drawn from 1/3, 2/5, 1/2,
// 3/5, 2/3, 7/10, 3/4, 4/5, never repeating on back-to-back days, so players
// cannot memorize one equilibrium. `frac` is what lib/outwit-score.js multiplies
// the pool mean by (it defaults to 2/3 for the pre-2026-07-21 days that predate
// the field). House arrays are shaped around that day's fraction. Days on or
// before 2026-07-20 are frozen as shipped: two-thirds, prompt first.
//
// THE HOUSE CROWD IS AN ESTIMATE, NOT A MEASUREMENT (stated plainly, 2026-09-05).
// Every `house` array in this file is the author's judgement about how a broad
// audience would answer, written out as votes. None of it is observed play. No
// board has ever been seeded from `outwit_picks`, and "generated by a seeded
// script; hand-shaped distributions" above means exactly that: a seeded script
// laid a hand-chosen vote ladder over a hand-chosen ranking of the options. It
// is a legitimate thing to ship, because `house` exists only so the first player
// of the day has a plausible field to be scored against, and lib/outwit-score
// retires it pool-wide once an eleventh real player arrives. It would NOT be
// legitimate to let it read as data about real players. If a future board is
// ever seeded from real picks, that board should say so and this note stops
// covering it.
//
// BOARDS FROM 2026-09-30 (num 76 on) are built by scripts/gen-outwit.mjs from
// the prompt pool in scripts/outwit-prompts.mjs, and they add rules the earlier
// boards were never held to. scripts/verify-daily-banks.mjs enforces all of it
// from that date and grandfathers everything before it:
//
//   house size    48 votes on every prompt, the number this header has always
//                 documented. Boards 17-75 ship 24; that is frozen history.
//   crowd shape   a prompt with no right answer still needs a FINDABLE crowd
//                 answer, so the distribution is banded. Meeting Point: the
//                 favorite takes 15-24 of the 48 and leads the runner-up by at
//                 least 4, with a runner-up of 10+ and a third of 7+. Road Less
//                 Traveled: the answer takes 4-8 and is at least 3 clear of the
//                 next-rarest, favorite 22 or less. Rare Bird: the two tail
//                 picks (both pay 2) sit at 2-4 and the third-rarest is at least
//                 2 above them, favorite 12 or less. NO OPTION EVER GETS ZERO
//                 VOTES: a zero-vote option cannot win a fewest/rarest prompt at
//                 all (lib/outwit-score), so it is a trap rather than an answer.
//   herd          the crowd's median is a whole reachable number, no single
//                 guess holds more than 45% of the pool, and the guesses fan out
//                 over at least eight values (five when the answer is under ten,
//                 where a real crowd genuinely converges). The crowd's median is
//                 deliberately NOT the true answer on most boards.
//   sunday        six prompts, the extra a second Rare Bird tagged "Rarer Bird"
//                 on its OWN theme, plus a crowd that is harder to read: every
//                 choice prompt on a Sunday drops one step flatter, so the
//                 favorite never exceeds 20 of 48 on a Meeting Point, 19 on a
//                 Road Less Traveled or 11 on a Rare Bird.
//   variety       no prompt text is ever reused in the bank; a category fills at
//                 most 8 of 62 boards in one slot and never two days running; no
//                 two prompts on one board share a category; a Meeting Point
//                 favorite heads at most 2 boards; an option string appears in at
//                 most 5 prompts; one house count vector shapes at most 12
//                 boards in a slot. Sundays get a REAL second Rare Bird, not the
//                 canned "Narrow it down" over the first prompt's own options
//                 that every Sunday from 2026-08-16 shipped.
//   copy          US spellings (CLAUDE.md authoring standard #8) and culture-
//                 broad subject matter. Boards 17-75 went British — colour,
//                 theatre, programme, Munros, crumpets, shillings, Cluedo — and
//                 stay that way, because the past is frozen.
